  "env GHX_ACCOUNT=jaguilar-century ghx pr create --repo century-inc/branchkinect-century-iac --base main --head feat/gke-ci-runners-pool --title \"feat(gke): add the ci-runners node pool to the nonprod cluster\" --body \"## Summary\n\nAdds a dedicated node pool, \\`ci-runners\\`, to the nonprod cluster \\`century-nonprod-gke\\`, so CI runner pods no longer compete with the app and voice workloads on \\`century-nonprod-gke-primary\\`.\n\n## Context\n\ncentury-inc/branchkinect-platform#1957 item 5 and #788: the ARC \\`e2e-gcp-arc\\` runners run on the app pool, request 250m/1Gi and peak at about 2 cores and 3.6 GiB. #283 tried this together with image streaming and a module repin to factory \\`v0.21.0\\`; that tag was never published and #283 is closed. This PR supersedes its runner-pool part only. century-inc/branchkinect-gitops-nonprod#325 removed a StatefulSet runner, not a node pool, so nothing here conflicts with it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New unit \\`environments/nonprod/platform/gke-ci-runners/\\` (local Terraform, same pattern as \\`platform/monitoring-gke\\`): one \\`google_container_node_pool\\` named \\`ci-runners\\`.\n  - \\`e2-standard-4\\`, standard VMs, boot disk \\`pd-standard\\` 100 GB, autoscaling 0-2 nodes in \\`us-central1-a\\` (inherited from the cluster), upgrade \\`max_surge 0\\` / \\`max_unavailable 1\\`.\n  - Node label \\`bk.workload=ci-runners\\` and taint \\`bk.workload=ci-runners:NoSchedule\\`.\n  - Same node service account, scopes, Workload Identity metadata and shielded settings as the primary pool.\n- \\`README.md\\`: the unit is listed in the layout.\n\n## How to deploy\n\nMerge. \\`backbone.yml\\` applies the new platform unit after \\`platform/gke\\`. The pool starts at 0 nodes. Runners use it only after the gitops change that adds the toleration and node selector for \\`bk.workload=ci-runners\\` to the \\`e2e-gcp-arc\\` scale set; until then nothing schedules there.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- The pinned module (factory \\`v0.17.0\\`) and every published tag up to \\`v0.20.0\\` declare a single pool and no additional-pools input, hence the local unit.\n- Primary pool settings were read live with gcloud to mirror its node identity and security settings.\n- The CI plan for \\`platform/gke-ci-runners\\` is the check for this PR: expected \\`1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy\\`. No other unit and no shared file changes, so no other unit is planned.\n\n## Risk and rollback\n\nThe pool lives in its own state, so this plan cannot touch the cluster or the primary pool. At full scale both pools reach exactly CPUS_ALL_REGIONS 32 (6 + 2 nodes x 4 vCPU), which is why surge is 0. To roll back, empty the pool of runner pods, then destroy the unit's resources before deleting the folder.\n\n## Technical notes\n\n- Quota on 2026-11-03: CPUS_ALL_REGIONS 24/32, SSD_TOTAL_GB 466/500, DISKS_TOTAL_GB 0/4096, PREEMPTIBLE_CPUS 0/0. \\`pd-standard\\` draws on DISKS_TOTAL_GB.\n- Spot was not used. Google's quota docs say Spot uses standard CPU quota only when the project has no preemptible quota and never requested any; whether it was ever requested cannot be confirmed here.\n- A longer-term option is an \\`additional_node_pools\\` input in factory \\`modules/gke\\`, after which this unit could move into \\`platform/gke\\`.\"": "Real approval (ghx pr create --repo century-inc/branchkinect-century-iac): opening a PR on a client repo; free under change-request-open, it runs nothing until merged."
